  "title": "The app catalog grew in several directions at once",
  "summary": "A community-heavy day: 66 app listings joined the catalog, while its links, categories, and submission flow got some attention.\n\nSixty-six community-app listings were added, spanning image and video tools, chatbots, games, learning apps, writing tools, and developer workflows. Among them are a RimWorld AI mod, an n8n node package for Pollinations image and text APIs, and an Android language-learning RPG. These PRs added catalog entries, not new Pollinations API features.\n\nThe app catalog now separates app names from web URLs, recovers more than 15 URLs from submissions, and drops 34 invalid repository URLs. Dev Tools, Vibes, and Social Bots now use matching category IDs on the Apps page, so their listings appear in the right places. The submission form also no longer requires people to choose an app category.\n\nCatGPT’s image requests and Model Monitor’s model lists were migrated to gen.pollinations.ai. AI Dungeon Master’s story requests now target the chat completions endpoint. The migration also changed its image URL construction, though the merged URL format differs from its README example.",
